[{"id":10151,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10151\">#1</a> When I click on a post in the discussion “2-Limits” from my feed reader, it takes me to a blank page that shows no comments.  But if I delete the parameter “&amp;page=2limits” from the URL, then the page displays as it should again.  <a href=\"http://www.math.ntnu.no/~stacey/Vanilla/nForum/comments.php?DiscussionID=1237&amp;page=2limits&amp;Focus=10159#Comment_10159\">Here</a> is the broken link. This only seems to happen with that particular discussion.  I’m guessing that maybe the forum software is getting confused by the “2” at the beginning and thinking that it should show the “second” page of comments, only there isn’t any such?</p>","timestamp":1273447487,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":10428,"sender_id":9,"sender_full_name":"Andrew Stacey","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/59e0a28758c4f6630d67fe7138b37311?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10428\">#2</a> I think I’ve fixed this.  I couldn’t see any reason why the page name was included in the URL, and it was being included in the place where the page <em>number</em> should have been so even if it should be in the URL somewhere, then that isn’t the right place.  Hopefully, this hasn’t broken anything else.</p>\n<p>(I’ll contact the writer of this particular extension to see what’s going on here)</p>\n<p>Please check that things are working as they should now.</p>","timestamp":1273762136,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":10429,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10429\">#3</a> If I click on the broken link Mike supplies I get the usual forum page, and ‘1 to 12 of 12’ top and bottom, but no comments in between them at all.</p>","timestamp":1273762429,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":10432,"sender_id":14,"sender_full_name":"TobyBartels","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac66e2e51d2a389b2ab9b2a99100a0c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10432\">#4</a> @ David:</p>\n<p>Yes, that’s what I get too.</p>\n<p>Andrew has not fixed this link (which was never correctly formed), but presumably he has fixed the feed so that it no longer produces this bad link?</p>","timestamp":1273766528,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":10434,"sender_id":9,"sender_full_name":"Andrew Stacey","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/59e0a28758c4f6630d67fe7138b37311?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10434\">#5</a> Wot Toby said.</p>","timestamp":1273766863,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":10435,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10435\">#6</a> Hard to test that until someone posts something at a discussion whose name begins with a number…</p>","timestamp":1273767923,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":10443,"sender_id":9,"sender_full_name":"Andrew Stacey","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/59e0a28758c4f6630d67fe7138b37311?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10443\">#7</a> It’s a bit odd that we didn’t see the bug earlier.  We’ve had lots and lots of discussions with titles like “∞-category of ∞-categories”.  Why didn’t they trigger it?</p>","timestamp":1273769680,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":10445,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10445\">#8</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We’ve had lots and lots of discussions with titles like “∞-category of ∞-categories”.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Alas, we have not arrived at that holy goal yet. We are still stuck with the <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-category of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\infty,1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-categories, mostly. ;-)</p>","timestamp":1273769883,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":10447,"sender_id":9,"sender_full_name":"Andrew Stacey","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/59e0a28758c4f6630d67fe7138b37311?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10447\">#9</a> Okay, I just added a comment at the discussion on 2-limits.  Did everything work as it should?</p>","timestamp":1273770599,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]},{"id":10452,"sender_id":10,"sender_full_name":"Mike Shulman","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ede34282f405f902e12fa7e6cf336572?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/17-n-Forum/topic/numbers.20in.20names/near/10452\">#10</a> Looks good to me; thanks!</p>","timestamp":1273777609,"subject":"numbers in names","stream_id":17,"display_recipient":"n-Forum","reactions":[]}]